WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.439 --> 00:00:07.439
ECHOSPACE turns ambient radio measurements into a 3D picture of a room. Everything here runs in the browser on a synthetic simulation.

2
00:00:07.443 --> 00:00:14.443
The overview shows the live session: source, processing state, a 3D preview and metrics measured from the running engine.

3
00:00:21.491 --> 00:00:29.491
Act 1. Eight transceivers line the walls. A synthetic person walks a scripted path, drawn as dashed white ground truth.

4
00:00:50.808 --> 00:00:58.808
Cyan lines are the modelled radio paths for one link: the direct path, wall reflections, and the scatter off the body.

5
00:00:59.415 --> 00:01:05.446
Act 2. RF Signal Studio. These plots come from the simulated channel state of the selected link, frame by frame.

6
00:01:05.446 --> 00:01:14.446
The Doppler spectrogram shows motion as spread energy. When the person stops or sits, it collapses back to the centre.

7
00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:22.480
Raw phase is scrambled by oscillator offsets. Sanitization removes a fitted linear phase so antenna differences survive.

8
00:01:22.514 --> 00:01:27.662
Act 3. The pipeline has twelve stages. Each one reports its input and output shapes and its measured run time.

9
00:01:27.662 --> 00:01:35.662
Spatial representation: a Bayesian radio tomography posterior over a voxel grid, computed in the dual form so it stays fast.

10
00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:44.700
Act 4. Back in the lab. Blue voxels and points are the model output. The violet sphere is a track with a two sigma ellipse.

11
00:01:44.926 --> 00:01:52.926
Amber marks voxels that no link can see. The system reports them as unknown instead of pretending they are empty.

12
00:01:54.466 --> 00:02:00.466
Act 5. We drop the signal to noise ratio to 3 dB and lose 40 percent of packets.

13
00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:09.467
Input quality falls, confidence drops and position error grows. The model is not allowed to hold on to an old answer.

14
00:02:09.846 --> 00:02:16.694
Act 6. Saving stores the seed, the launch configuration, every mid run change, model versions and measured metrics.

15
00:02:16.694 --> 00:02:25.694
The experiment page lists provenance and metric summaries. Replay relaunches the run and checks a digest of its first forty frames.

16
00:02:26.015 --> 00:02:33.015
The digest matches, so the run was reproduced exactly from its saved configuration.

17
00:02:33.016 --> 00:02:39.016
That is the whole loop: simulate, measure, reconstruct, fail honestly, save, and reproduce.
